```c
if (total_allocated < size) {
    err = -ENOSPC;
    goto err_free;
}
```
Reason:
The `alloc_range()` function did not properly check if the total allocated size met the requested size before returning success. This oversight allowed the function to return a success status even when the memory allocation was insufficient, leading to display corruption.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (total_allocated < size) {
    err = -ENOSPC;
    goto err_free;
}
```
Reason:
The patch adds a check to ensure that if the total allocated size is less than the required size, the function will return an error code `-ENOSPC`. This change ensures that the function accurately reflects the success of the memory allocation, preventing incorrect behavior and display corruption.

